{"id": "EUVD-2026-67492", "enisaUuid": "29279208-e85f-3c54-90fa-695c9f5e431d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: Avoid calling WARN_ON() on -ENOMEM in cfg802154_switch_netns()\n\nIt's pointless to call WARN_ON() in case of an allocation failure in\ndev_change_net_namespace() and device_rename(), since it only leads to\nuseless splats caused by deliberate fault injections, so avoid it.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with Syzkaller.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c67e70202cfd602f86d3e59fe6fffecaf4110f40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f300e68014cf10af9aa0c0ad958750a8509c8e44", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4860dd988b1041d70595f2ed84de80f90cb7ebc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fcba77571c53f656a2f109259601a7570d4c74a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0569f67ed6a7af838e2141da93c68e6b6013f483"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hccx-rj7h-28cw", "CVE-2026-80616"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0545181e-a70b-370d-992c-fcd95091243e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66e5c2672cd11b9310008099faf6a4ffb9dfb6d0 <f4860dd988b1041d70595f2ed84de80f90cb7ebc"}, {"id": "0bada0f6-3f8e-32cf-b314-a2639e00e6d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "30434f57-6f53-33de-b1e9-10f097db9733", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66e5c2672cd11b9310008099faf6a4ffb9dfb6d0 <6fcba77571c53f656a2f109259601a7570d4c74a"}, {"id": "37387a6e-cf1d-30e7-9baf-3ebbc0500376", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5b13c2aa-6b45-3051-940d-a041e47bd9ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66e5c2672cd11b9310008099faf6a4ffb9d